Here is how you can manage your live environment settings on Render.

Managing Your Live Environment Variables
#
Option A: Keep Using Mock Data (For Demos)

If you want to use this link as a safe portfolio demo to show other people how the charts work without connecting a real bank account:

You do not need to change anything! The app will continue reading the static JSON backup files.
#
Option B: Connect to Real Azure Cloud Data If you want this dashboard to show real costs for a business or your personal account, you need to inject your secure Azure credentials directly into Render:
#
1. Open your Render Dashboard.
#
2. Click on your Backend Web Service from the list.
#
3. Click on Environment in the left menu.
#
4. Click Add Environment Variable and add your specific Azure API connection keys:

   A. AZURE_TENANT_ID

   B. AZURE_CLIENT_ID
   
   C. AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET
#
5. Change MOCK_DATA to false.
#
6. Click Save Changes. Render will automatically restart your server and connect securely to Azure.

A Quick Reminder on Live Deletions Because this specific dashboard application contains code features that can delete virtual machines or change resource sizes, be extremely careful if you switch MOCK_DATA to false on a live production subscription. Make sure any users logging into your live onrender.com link have the correct permissions so no critical business servers are modified by accident.
